      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Pemphigus vulgaris most often begins in the mouth but is often overlooked in the differential diagnosis of chronic, multiple oral ulcerations and erosions. Accurate diagnosis requires perilesional biopsy including intact epithelium, submitted for hematoxylin and eosin as well as direct immunofluorescence staining. Early and aggressive treatment with moderate to high dose prednisone in combination with steroid sparing drugs such as azathioprine and mycophenolate allow complete remission in most patients."},
